From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kan Zhu <kanzhu@cs.washington.edu>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 21:16:47 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] docs(alignment): rebase the line onto upstream 5629b26 for
 DeepSeek-V4.1 DSpark

Record the new upstream base (main 5629b26146, 2026-11-07, with a cu130
precompiled wheel), the wheel commit for the environment, and the
commits adapted to upstream changes. No commit was dropped.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 ALIGNMENT.md | 61 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++------------
 1 file changed, 47 insertions(+), 14 deletions(-)

diff --git a/ALIGNMENT.md b/ALIGNMENT.md
index 738347cc20544909fa6da0ff7a7b884a54aa3870..b2c3e393a391ce98f1d95d5f68b1c8fa31a72f3f 100644
--- a/ALIGNMENT.md
+++ b/ALIGNMENT.md
@@ -2,15 +2,46 @@
 
 `servingstudio-alignment` is the one maintained ServingStudio line of this fork.
 It sits on official vLLM `upstream/main`; the current upstream base is main
-`04730e82700d0c9b957cda188dd1bbc8073e1fcd` (2026-09-24). That is the newest
-main commit with a published `cu130` precompiled wheel that contains
-`vllm/models/deepseek_v41`, so DeepSeek-V4.1 can be served. ServingStudio Sim
-pins the line at `alignment/profiler/vllm`.
-
-The line was previously based on `8369affa5428ca29a30f378d660fbffbad12e240`
-(v0.28.1rc0). The rebase onto `04730e8` kept one commit per instrumentation
-commit, except `Bind AsyncLLM.profiler on every profiler backend`. That commit
-is dropped because upstream `c3ec0d29f5` binds `AsyncLLM.profiler` itself.
+`5629b26146a39705c814ddae6a0f98321e14d2a6` (2026-11-07). It has a published
+`cu130` precompiled wheel and carries DeepSeek-V4.1 with its DSpark drafter
+(`vllm/models/deepseek_v41/nvidia/dspark.py`,
+`vllm/v1/worker/gpu/spec_decode/dspark/`). ServingStudio Sim pins the line at
+`alignment/profiler/vllm`.
+
+Earlier bases were `04730e82700d0c9b957cda188dd1bbc8073e1fcd` (main,
+2026-09-24) and `8369affa5428ca29a30f378d660fbffbad12e240` (v0.28.1rc0). The
+rebase onto `04730e8` dropped `Bind AsyncLLM.profiler on every profiler
+backend`, because upstream `c3ec0d29f5` binds `AsyncLLM.profiler` itself.
+
+The rebase onto `5629b26` kept all 17 commits, one for one. These commits were
+adapted to upstream changes:
+
+- `restore iteration and expert profiling`: upstream now copies EPLB
+  balancedness stats to the host without blocking and logs them on a later
+  step. `VibeSimAlignmentExpertLoad` follows the same path. The logical counts
+  are copied with the balancedness stats, and the record is logged when that
+  copy completes. `observed_monotonic_ns` is still taken at the observed step.
+  The record of the last logged step before shutdown can be lost.
+- `decompose API-side request latency`: the two API timing arguments are
+  optional keywords, so upstream callers and tests do not pass them. Completions
+  also time upstream's templated plain-delta frames. Token-in/token-out counts
+  only chunks that carry tokens; upstream now also streams terminal and
+  held-back-text chunks.
+- `record Spec5 request and expert evidence`: `EplbState.add_model` keeps
+  upstream's `model_name` and adds `model_role` and `max_forwards_per_step` as
+  keyword arguments. The V2 EPLB test's DSpark speculator stub now has
+  `num_speculative_tokens`.
+- `instrument upstream model runner v2 for DFlash2`: the phase scopes were
+  applied again to upstream's runner. `step_timing.record_batch` and
+  `forward_start` are inside `preprocess`. The routing capturer binds after
+  `initialize_output_storage`, because upstream creates the AuxOutput connector
+  in `profile_run`.
+- `add a record-only mode that never rearranges`: this commit adapts
+  upstream's `symm_mem` communicator-owned expert buffer.
+- `capture the MTP drafter's routes under model runner V2`: upstream split the
+  autoregressive speculator. The hold and restore of the drafter's slots now
+  wrap `AutoRegressiveSpeculator._run_multi_step_decode`, which MTP uses
+  through `TargetDependentARSpeculator`.
 
 It converges two earlier lines:
 
@@ -53,7 +84,7 @@ or native extensions. The installation used:
 ```bash
 uv venv --python 3.12 .venv
 VLLM_USE_PRECOMPILED=1 \
-VLLM_PRECOMPILED_WHEEL_COMMIT=04730e82700d0c9b957cda188dd1bbc8073e1fcd \
+VLLM_PRECOMPILED_WHEEL_COMMIT=5629b26146a39705c814ddae6a0f98321e14d2a6 \
 VLLM_PRECOMPILED_WHEEL_VARIANT=cu130 \
 uv pip install --python .venv/bin/python -e .
 uv pip install --python .venv/bin/python -r requirements/lint.txt \
@@ -62,7 +93,7 @@ uv pip check --python .venv/bin/python
 ```
 
 `VLLM_PRECOMPILED_WHEEL_COMMIT` must be the upstream base SHA,
-`04730e82700d0c9b957cda188dd1bbc8073e1fcd`. If the upstream base changes,
+`5629b26146a39705c814ddae6a0f98321e14d2a6`. If the upstream base changes,
 update the wheel commit explicitly. Import and
 GPU validation must resolve Python and native extensions under this worktree.
 An import check alone does not qualify the driver or a serving run.
@@ -72,7 +103,7 @@ default. Run pre-commit checks explicitly in this checkout; do not replace
 shared Git hooks with a hook that points at this environment.
 
 The wheel saved in `../glm53-dflash2-artifacts/` is the `cu130` wheel for the
-earlier `8369aff` base. It does not match `04730e8`, so do not use it with this
+earlier `8369aff` base. It does not match `5629b26`, so do not use it with this
 base. If that metadata endpoint is
 temporarily unavailable, set `VLLM_PRECOMPILED_WHEEL_LOCATION` to the path in
 `vllm-wheel-path.txt`. `native-wheel.json` records its SHA256 and provenance.
@@ -110,7 +141,7 @@ checkpoint compatibility in a full vLLM run still requires validation.
 
 ServingStudio's `token_corpus` pass serves with `--enable-return-routed-experts`
 and reads every generated token's routes, body layers and MTP layer. At
-`04730e8`, upstream serves routes through the AuxOutput connector
+`5629b26`, upstream serves routes through the AuxOutput connector
 (`vllm/distributed/aux_output_connector/`). The connector requires Model Runner
 V2, a MoE generate model, and prefix caching. It rejects adaptive speculative
 verification, PP > 1, DCP/PCP > 1, and KV connectors. Upstream also captures
@@ -126,7 +157,9 @@ branch adds:
   propose. `AsyncOutput.copy_aux_output` then starts the step's deferred D2H
   copy.
 
-V1 cannot return routes at this base. The routing dump
+Drafter slots exist only for method `mtp`. The DSpark drafter's MoE routes
+are not captured or returned; only the target's are. V1 cannot return routes at
+this base. The routing dump
 (`VLLM_VIBESIM_ROUTING_TRACE_*`) still works on both runners. On V1, and on V2
 without the connector, the dump's env var binds a private capturer that returns
 nothing on responses. The dump skips the drafter's slots.
